course: dictionary
lesson: 3381
title: Existence
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Existence is a noun. It means being real, or being alive, or the fact that something is there. «The existence of dinosaurs is proved by fossils.» The fossils show that dinosaurs were real.
explain: You can also talk about things that start or stop existing. To come into existence means to start, and to go out of existence means to end. Ask yourself: is the sentence about something being real, or starting or ending?
explain: Existence can also mean a way of living, especially a hard or dull one. «He led a lonely existence.» The word lonely is the clue: it tells you the life was dull and sad, not that the man was not real. When you meet existence, try both meanings and see which one fits the sentence.
fact: Existence means being real or being alive.
fact: «Come into existence» means start, and «go out of existence» means end.
fact: «A lonely existence» or «a miserable existence» describes a hard or unhappy way of living.
fact: The liar's dividend means people use the existence of fakes to deny things that really happened.
fact: A good check is to swap in another word, such as being or life, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The existence of dinosaurs is proved by fossils.» What does existence mean here? | A dull way of living | *Being real | Being very old | Being hungry
exercise: «He led a lonely existence on the farm.» What does existence mean here? | Starting to be | *A hard or dull way of living | Being real | Ending for good
exercise: What does the phrase «come into existence» mean? | Get very wet | *Start to be | Go to sleep | End for good
test: Which phrase means that something stops being? | Come into existence | *Go out of existence | The existence of fossils | A miserable existence
test: Which best describes «a miserable existence»? | *A hard, unhappy life | A life spent at the seaside | Being real and alive | A happy, busy life
exam: «People use the existence of fakes to deny things that really happened.» In this sentence, existence means | *The fact that the fakes are real | Starting to be made | Being very old | A dull way of living
